      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “familiar” (or “spatial familiarity”) as having prior knowledge/experience of a place or as “feels more known than new.” The text only states that the parks “differ[ed] in familiarity” without giving a definitional description.",
        "The claim “Lower familiarity with a setting was linked to more negative emotional responses in the study” is supported: the packet reports a main effect where lower familiarity was associated with increased negative affect (NA). However, because the definitional portion is not supported, the overall definition cannot be accepted."
